pleted pivots: 0\n- Failed pivots: 0\n- Audited overrides: 0\n- Saturated: none yet\n- Pivot lineage: none yet\n- Remaining frontier: none recorded\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:divergent-pivots -->\n<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n## 7. NEXT FOCUS\nWhich exact Devin ACP and Claude MessageDisplay fields vary by installed version?\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n<!-- ANCHOR:active-risks -->\n## 8. ACTIVE RISKS\n- None active beyond normal research uncertainty.\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:active-risks -->\n<!-- ANCHOR:blocked-stops -->\n## 9. BLOCKED STOPS\nNo blocked-stop events recorded.\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:blocked-stops -->\n<!-- ANCHOR:graph-convergence -->\n## 10. GRAPH CONVERGENCE\n- graphConvergenceScore: 0.00\n- graphDecision: [Not recorded]\n- graphBlockers: none recorded\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:graph-convergence -->","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":114,"totalLines":114,"truncated":false}},"title":"specs/cli-external-orchestration/042-improved-communication/001-research-strategy/research/lineages/gpt-sol-fast/deep-research-dashboard.md","time":{"start":1786433672645,"end":1786433672660}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_01f4d7aa3449db22016a7ad088697c8191af22cc3f103fae00"}},"id":"prt_fefbe95c3001Pxd20icDy049fS","sessionID":"ses_010495952ffeknG4pENad6KM6w","messageID":"msg_fefbe72c70011ZohaR8qLaQ3wh"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1786433672665,"sessionID":"ses_010495952ffeknG4pENad6KM6w","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_miIJB37les8k4cUIYA6U1uz5","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/0138-system-deep-loop-communication-research/specs/cli-external-orchestration/042-improved-communication/001-research-strategy/research/lineages/gpt-sol-fast/deep-research-strategy.md"},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/0138-system-deep-loop-communication-research/specs/cli-external-orchestration/042-improved-communication/001-research-strategy/research/lineages/gpt-sol-fast/deep-research-strategy.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Deep Research Strategy: Provider-Neutral CLI Display Projection\n2: \n3: ## 2. TOPIC\n4: Reverse engineer claudish-to-english and derive an evidence-backed, provider-neutral display-projection architecture that preserves canonical runtime state while matching its direct 1:1 communication feel across Claude CLI, Codex CLI, Pi CLI, OpenCode CLI, Devin CLI, and Cursor CLI.\n5: \n6: <!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n7: ## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\n8: - [x] What is the safest primary-source-supported display integration boundary in each of the six CLIs, and how should their events normalize without mutating canonical context, tools, or transcripts?\n9: - [ ] How should message assembly handle streaming, ordering, duplication, concurrency, cancellation, timeout, retry, and atomic render commitment?\n10: - [ ] Which protected-span and semantic fidelity gates can reject every changed literal, structure, fact, polarity, requirement strength, caveat, or next step and return the exact original?\n11: - [ ] How should privacy-aware routing normalize OpenCode Go DeepSeek V4 Flash, Ollama, llama.cpp, and other hosted or local providers without unapproved egress or capability assumptions?\n12: - [ ] Which observability, perceptual-parity evaluation, and downstream phase boundaries make the architecture testable and implementable?\n13: \n14: <!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n15: \n16: ## 4. NON-GOALS\n17: - No production implementation, provider configuration, package installation, service startup, or deployment.\n18: - No mutation of canonical model context, tool events, tool results, transcript state, or the read-only reference.\n19: - No claim that protocol compatibility alone proves privacy, fidelity, or safe presentation replacement.\n20: - No writes outside this detached lineage packet.\n21: \n22: ## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n23: - Complete exactly three evidence iterations, regardless of early convergence telemetry.\n24: - Stop on an unrecoverable state or scope violation and preserve the partial packet honestly.\n25: \n26: <!-- ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n27: ## 6. ANSWERED QUESTIONS\n28: - What is the safest primary-source-supported display integration boundary in each of the six CLIs, and how should their events normalize without mutating canonical context, tools, or transcripts?\n29: \n30: <!-- /ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n31: \n32: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n33: <!-- ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n34: ## 7. WHAT WORKED\n35: - runtime-owned client protocols exposed identity, lifecycle, cancellation, and terminal states more completely than hooks, while Claude’s dedicated display hook provided the useful narrow exception. (iteration 1)\n36: \n37: <!-- /ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n38: \n39: <!-- ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n40: ## 8. WHAT FAILED\n41: - broad rendered pages produced oversized captures, and one assumed ACP documentation route did not exist. Raw primary documents and runtime-specific pages were more reliable. (iteration 1)\n42: \n43: <!-- /ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n44: \n45: <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n46: ## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n47: ### `https://agentclientprotocol.com/protocol/session-updates` returned 404. No claims de