2-4\",\"summary\":\"Projection commit is a one-time compare-and-swap after successful source terminal status and all validators; every other path retains original.\",\"status\":\"partial\",\"sources\":[\"specs/cli-external-orchestration/042-improved-communication/001-research-strategy/research/lineages/gpt-sol-fast/iterations/iteration-001.md:30\",\"https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/server-sent-events.html\"]}\n6: {\"type\":\"finding\",\"iteration\":2,\"id\":\"finding-2-5\",\"summary\":\"Protected spans combine pinned Markdown source ranges with conservative literal lexing and placeholder bijection/order checks.\",\"status\":\"new\",\"sources\":[\"https://spec.commonmark.org/0.31.2/\"]}\n7: {\"type\":\"finding\",\"iteration\":2,\"id\":\"finding-2-6\",\"summary\":\"Validation runs deterministic completion, placeholder, byte, and AST gates before veto-only semantic checks.\",\"status\":\"new\",\"sources\":[\"https://genai.owasp.org/llmrisk/llm01-prompt-injection/\",\"https://spec.commonmark.org/0.31.2/\"]}\n8: {\"type\":\"finding\",\"iteration\":2,\"id\":\"finding-2-7\",\"summary\":\"Exact fallback retains pre-parse canonical bytes because parsing and UTF-8 stream decoding can erase source distinctions.\",\"status\":\"partial\",\"sources\":[\"https://spec.commonmark.org/0.31.2/\",\"https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/server-sent-events.html\"]}\n9: {\"type\":\"ruled_out\",\"iteration\":2,\"id\":\"ruled-out-2-1\",\"summary\":\"Arrival order as canonical assembly order\",\"sources\":[\"https://www.jsonrpc.org/specification\",\"https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/server-sent-events.html\"]}\n10: {\"type\":\"ruled_out\",\"iteration\":2,\"id\":\"ruled-out-2-2\",\"summary\":\"Reconstructing exact original from parsed or transformed text\",\"sources\":[\"https://spec.commonmark.org/0.31.2/\",\"https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/server-sent-events.html\"]}\n11: {\"type\":\"ruled_out\",\"iteration\":2,\"id\":\"ruled-out-2-3\",\"summary\":\"Treating an LLM judge as deterministic semantic proof\",\"sources\":[\"https://genai.owasp.org/llmrisk/llm01-prompt-injection/\"]}\n12: {\"type\":\"ruled_out\",\"iteration\":2,\"id\":\"ruled-out-2-4\",\"summary\":\"Suppressing original chunks before successful validation\",\"sources\":[\"specs/cli-external-orchestration/042-improved-communication/001-research-strategy/research/lineages/gpt-sol-fast/iterations/iteration-001.md:30\"]}\n\n(End of file - total 12 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"{\"type\":\"iteration\",\"iteration\":2,\"mode\":\"research\",\"target_agent\":\"deep-research\",\"agent_definition_loaded\":true,\"resolved_route\":\"Resolved route: mode=research target_agent=deep-research\",\"run\":2,\"status\":\"complete\",\"focus\":\"Version-aware streaming assembly state machine and layered protected-span/semantic fidelity validation\",\"findingsCount\":7,\"newInfoRatio\":0.86,\"noveltyJustification\":\"5 of 7 findings were fully new and 2 were partially new extensions of iteration 1's immutable event mirror.\",\"keyQuestions\":[\"How should message assembly handle streaming, ordering, duplication, concurrency, cancellation, timeout, retry, and atomic render commitment?\",\"Which protected-span and semantic fidelity gates can reject changed literals, structure, facts, polarity, requirement strength, caveats, or next steps and return the exact original?\"],\"answeredQuestions\":[\"A version-aware per-key assembly state machine with generation-safe retry, bounded backpressure, terminal fallback, and atomic commit was established at architecture-selection level.\",\"A deterministic-first protected-span and structural validator with veto-only semantic checks and immutable-byte fallback was established at architecture-selection level.\"],\"ruledOut\":[\"Arrival order as canonical assembly order\",\"Reconstructing exact original from parsed or transformed text\",\"Treating an LLM judge as deterministic semantic proof\",\"Suppressing original chunks before successful validat